## Shared understanding (do not re-litigate without Max)

### Sequence
C2 (single-writer claim) → C3 (liveness policy) → C1 (DeliveryEndpoint hybrid)

### C2 — C2c_kimi_delivery_claim
- Claim-before-POST, per-message, broker-local, 30s TTL
- Both notifier + deliver-service call claim
- On fail: skip msg, leave in inbox
- Call site: inside shared run_once after system-event partition, before POST
- Winner releases after successful POST; failed POST releases for retry

### C3 — C2c_liveness
- New module: state reg→Alive|Dead|Unknown + is_alive_for purpose
- Purposes: Delivery, Nudge, List, Sweep, Doctor
- Doctor uses for pid/liveness; wake class stays separate
- Facade-first migration; purpose-semantics tests first

### C1 — DELIVERY_ENDPOINT (hybrid first cut)
- Module type: probe / deliver / drain_policy
- Registry table; kimi first real adapter
- Mode_* temporary until ≥2 adapters
- Derive endpoint from registration (optional field later)
- Kimi path uses C2 claim; adapter declares drain_policy

## Explicit non-goals for first land
- Full Mode_* deletion day one
- Changing Unknown→Alive collapse semantics in C3
- Generalizing claim beyond kimi before second client needs it


